clk: qcom: gcc-sm7150: keep the QUPv3 wrapper AHB clocks always on

On the POCO X3 NFC (surya) the SoC stops dead, with no trace at all, within
a few seconds of gcc_qupv3_wrap_0_{m,s}_ahb_clk being gated. Measured on
2026-09-08: the wrapper's last active serial engine is the Bluetooth UART;
when it closes (bluetoothd powering the adapter off, rfkill, bootmac's MAC
cycle) and its siblings (touchscreen SPI, haptics and NFC I2C) are
runtime-suspended, geni_se_resources_off() drops the wrapper AHB clocks and
the phone freezes until the watchdog fires - sometimes not even that.
Keeping any sibling runtime-active (so the AHB clocks stay on) makes the very
same sequence survive; putting the siblings back to runtime-suspend, with no
bus traffic at all, kills it within 3 s. The persistent console of an
instrumented run ends exactly at the clk_disable of those two clocks.

The wrapper is a client of apps_smmu (iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x203 0x0>); a
master that cannot respond while the SMMU broadcasts TLB invalidations for
the display, GPU, camera and modem is the most plausible way to hang every
CPU silently. Until that is understood properly, mark the wrapper AHB clocks
critical, as several other gcc drivers do for bus clocks whose gating is not
safe. The cost is two AHB clocks per QUP wrapper never gating.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm7150.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm7150.c
@@ -2001,6 +2001,7 @@
 		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 			.name = "gcc_qupv3_wrap_0_m_ahb_clk",
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		},
 	},
 };
@@ -2016,6 +2017,7 @@
 		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 			.name = "gcc_qupv3_wrap_0_s_ahb_clk",
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		},
 	},
 };
@@ -2029,6 +2031,7 @@
 		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 			.name = "gcc_qupv3_wrap_1_m_ahb_clk",
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		},
 	},
 };
@@ -2044,6 +2047,7 @@
 		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 			.name = "gcc_qupv3_wrap_1_s_ahb_clk",
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
+			.flags = CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		},
